script:pre-request {
  // Send the global API key secret on /api/v1/* when it is set.
  // Leave apiKey empty to use the session cookie from Auth / Login instead.
  const apiKey = bru.getEnvVar("apiKey");
  const url = req.getUrl();
  if (apiKey && url.includes("/api/v1/") && !url.includes("/api/v1/api-keys")) {
    req.setHeader("X-API-Key", apiKey);
  }
}

docs {
  # Uptime Kuma Nuxt API — Bruno collection

  A small, curated smoke/CRUD collection for this deployment. Requests tagged
  `smoke` are read-only; create/update/delete requests are intended for the
  Local environment only.

  1. Select **Local** (http://localhost:32400) or **Production**
     (https://uptime.226network.com). Use Production for `smoke` requests only.
  2. Authenticate either by:
     - setting the `password` secret and running **Auth / Login** (Bruno keeps
       the `nuxt-session` cookie), or
     - setting the `apiKey` secret (`gk_...`, from Settings → Security → Global API key).
       It is sent as `X-API-Key` on `/api/v1/*` only. Auth, settings and
       API-key management endpoints still require the session cookie.
  3. "Create ..." requests store the new id in a variable (`monitorId`, `tagId`)
     used by the matching get/delete requests.

  Read-only smoke run: `bru run --env Production --tags smoke`

  Note: the in-app Bruno monitor type runs declarative `.bru` requests only —
  scripts and tests are stripped by the parser. Use the Bruno CLI for the
  pre-request script and assertions in this collection.
}
